# Stage 1 for stars on the CPU, quick: 2,000 synthetic stars (a quarter of them planted near-misses, so that rows exist)
# against 4,087 synthetic clusters, the size of the real cluster file. The first 2,000 stars of screen-long.wu.
# Why: stage 1 is most of the project's compute (33.8 million stars), and on the CPU almost all of it should be the chi2
# scan, ph_screen_chi2, over every (star, cluster, track point) with its two quad_inv calls and a segment test. The
# cluster precompute (4,087 ph_lin_cluster, once per task) and the star's own lin_integrate are the other fixed and
# per-star parts. A change to the scan shows here; a change to the integrator or the potential shows mostly in pulsar.wu.
# Header: chi2_max 25, n_samp 64 and r_kernel 2 are the defaults of src/phygas_screen.c, p_min 0.001 is the cut of the
# first full-size task in README.md; the server's real header is not in this repository.
# Expected on an Apple M1: 30-60 s (about 0.02 s per star against 4,087 clusters, the figure in docs/kb/ledger.md for
# PAT-007, plus 1-2 s of cluster precompute). Expected, not measured.
header PHYGAS 1 screen 25 64 2 0.001
clusters 4087
targets 2000
kind S
seed 1
